{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! Now I can see:\n\nFrom farmers_markets:\n- state_name (string)\n- state_abbr (string)\n- farmers_markets (int64) - the count of farmers markets per state\n- ... other fields\n\nFrom census_population:\n- NAME (string) - state name\n- SUMLEV (int64) - summary level\n- POPESTIMATE2025 (int64) - population estimate for 2025\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Get the total number of farmers markets from farmers_markets\n2. Get the total population from census_population (summing across states)\n3. Calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n4. Create a derived metric alias that calculates this ratio\n5. Use xorq_select to get the value\n6. Verify with xorq_verify\n\nLet me first peek at the data to understand how to aggregate it properly. I should check if the census data has a US total row or if I need to sum state-level data.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now let me peek at the data to understand the structure better:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_015duwqJi5ikgLXHZAhQak4f","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"census_population","compose":"source.filter(source.SUMLEV == 10).limit(1)","limit":5}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_012XRjyjaZAUPMeNF2VBH8A4","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers_markets","compose":"source.limit(5)","limit":5}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":481,"cacheRead":21777,"cacheWrite":1462,"totalTokens":23734,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.002405,"cacheRead":0.0021777000000000003,"cacheWrite":0.0018275,"total":0.006424200000000001},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":231},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915357375,"responseId":"msg_011Ce78UurxBk4M1b2Drzvks","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_015duwqJi5ikgLXHZAhQak4f","toolName":"xorq_select","